# Backend Setup

    ## Mongo DB Setup:
    1. Go to https://cloud.mongodb.com/atlas
    2. Create a Project
    3. Create a Free Cluster
        - Choose free cluster
        - Add a provider
        - Add name for the cluster
    4. Create a DB user
        - Go to "Database Access" tab in left side > Add New DB User
        - Chooose and set username and password
        - set privlage > Atlas admin
    5. Allow network access
        - Go to "Network Access" tab in left side > Add IP address
        - Add IP as "0.0.0.0/0" to allow access from anywhere
    6. Get the connection string
        - Cluster > Connect
        - Copy the connection string  (replace <password> with the db user password)

    ## Create a S3 Bucket

    ## Save the IAM user "Access ID" & "Secret Access Key"

    ## Streaming Service Setup
        - inside the "streamingService" create a .env file and add the following
            PORT=3002
            AWS_KEY_ID='<ur-acces-id>'
            AWS_SECRET_KEY='<ur-secret-key>'
            AWS_REGION='ca-central-1'
            AWS_S3_BUCKET='<ur-created-s3-bucket-name>'
            MONGO_URI="<mongo-db-uri-string>"
        - npm start

    ## Auth Service Setup
        - inside the "authService" create a .env file and add the following
            PORT=3001
            MONGO_URI="<mongo-db-uri-string>"
            JWT_SECRET="writesomerandomsecrets"
            AWS_KEY_ID='<ur-acces-id>'
            AWS_SECRET_KEY='<ur-secret-key>'
            AWS_REGION='ca-central-1'
            AWS_S3_BUCKET='<ur-created-s3-bucket-name>'
        - npm start
